      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Royal Brewery on Princess Road began life as a tram depot in 1909 and served Stagecoach Manchester until 2010.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moss_Side",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Originally the Albert Brewery, the site became known as Moss Side Brewery by 1915, cementing the area's brewing heritage.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moss_Side",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Moss Side hosts two Roman Catholic churches: the Polish‑founded Church of Divine Mercy on Moss Lane East and the 1949 Church of Our Lady of Perpetual Succour.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
